  "about": "Shared byte for byte by the R and Python suites of scopusflow. counts lists record sets as a year column, null for a record without a year, with the plan attached to each. One also carries the attributes of a harvest stopped before its last cell, which searched only the cells it ran. years and n are the year counts both twins return for it: R's internal scopus_year_counts(), which autoplot() draws, and Python's year_counts(). Every year a plan searched is counted, a year without records as zero, and no other year is added, so a year no cell searched never appears as a zero. Without a plan, or with one that sent no year limit, the years run from the first year in the records to the last. notes lists the years a record-count figure plots, the retrieval time recorded with its counts (in UTC) and the note both twins add to the figure, or null where they add none.",
